SELECT statements that return a single result row can also be executed using EXEC SQL directly. To handle result sets with multiple rows, an application has to use a cursor; see Section 36.3.2 below.

The steps to use a cursor are the following: declare a cursor, open it, fetch a row
from the cursor, repeat, and finally close it. Select using cursors:
EXEC SQL DECLARE foo_bar CURSOR FOR
