EXEC SQL OPEN foo_bar;
EXEC SQL FETCH foo_bar INTO :FooBar, DooDad;
... EXEC SQL CLOSE foo_bar;
EXEC SQL COMMIT;
For more details about declaring a cursor, see DECLARE; for more details about fetching rows from
a cursor, see FETCH. Note
The ECPG DECLARE command does not actually cause a statement to be sent to the Post-
greSQL backend.

