EXEC SQL END DECLARE SECTION;
... EXEC SQL START TRANSACTION;
ECPG will report a syntax error for START TRANSACTION, because it no longer recognizes START
as an SQL keyword, only as a typedef. (If you have such a conflict, and renaming the typedef seems
impractical, you could write the SQL command using dynamic SQL.)
Note
In PostgreSQL releases before v16, use of SQL keywords as typedef names was likely to result
in syntax errors associated with use of the typedef itself, rather than use of the name as an
SQL keyword.

The new behavior is less likely to cause problems when an existing ECPG
application is recompiled in a new PostgreSQL release with new keywords. 36.4.4.3.4. Pointers
