The pgtypes library maps PostgreSQL database types to C equivalents that can be used in C programs. It also offers functions to do basic calculations with those types within C, i.e., without the help of the
PostgreSQL server. See the following example:
EXEC SQL BEGIN DECLARE SECTION;
