The general steps to use an SQLDA to pass input parameters to a prepared query are:
1. Create a prepared query (prepared statement)
2. Declare an sqlda_t structure as an input SQLDA. 3.

Allocate memory area (as sqlda_t structure) for the input SQLDA. 4. Set (copy) input values in the allocated memory. 5. Open a cursor with specifying the input SQLDA. Here is an example. First, create a prepared statement. EXEC SQL BEGIN DECLARE SECTION;
